{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600352",
      "title": "Frontend Code vs Backend Code",
      "sourceHash": "be7bb2b2ef0733bbfa28f492d4c029b6081675e8c0a2edf7ff9eeb92b9589312",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.06,
          "end": 6.01,
          "en": "And let's start with running the async code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.01,
          "end": 9.77,
          "en": "the side effect inside of our components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.77,
          "end": 12.85,
          "en": "Let's maybe start with adding items to a card",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.85,
          "end": 15.92,
          "en": "from inside the product item component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.92,
          "end": 20.35,
          "en": "That means that in here we have this add to cart handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.35,
          "end": 24.02,
          "en": "and we could of course then not just dispatch an action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.02,
          "end": 28.27,
          "en": "to our Redux store but we could also send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.27,
          "end": 32.16,
          "en": "that data to Firebase to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.16,
          "end": 34.73,
          "en": "We would just have one problem with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.73,
          "end": 38.69,
          "en": "If we just send the product data to Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.69,
          "end": 41.01,
          "en": "So the data which we're sending to Redux here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.01,
          "end": 43.71,
          "en": "if we just sent that to Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.71,
          "end": 47.65,
          "en": "we would just store that product data in Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.65,
          "end": 52.43,
          "en": "but Firebase the way we are using it does not have any logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.43,
          "end": 54.47,
          "en": "on its own on the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.47,
          "end": 59.17,
          "en": "So on the Firebase backend we don't run any extra code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.17,
          "end": 61.84,
          "en": "So if we send some product data there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.84,
          "end": 65.97,
          "en": "that product data would simply be added to the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.97,
          "end": 68.44,
          "en": "but all the logic we have in the reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.44,
          "end": 72.65,
          "en": "for checking whether a product is already part of the cart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.65,
          "end": 77.03,
          "en": "and if it is updating as quantity, if it's not adding it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 77.03,
          "end": 81.36,
          "en": "that kind of logic simply does not run on Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 81.36,
          "end": 84.66,
          "en": "because that's a pretty dumb backend here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 84.66,
          "end": 86.11,
          "en": "the way we're using it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 86.11,
          "end": 89.12,
          "en": "and therefore we don't have such logic there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 89.12,
          "end": 92.97,
          "en": "Now if you would be using Firebase for a real project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.97,
          "end": 95.82,
          "en": "you could add server side code to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.82,
          "end": 98.15,
          "en": "There is a service called functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.15,
          "end": 100.52000000000001,
          "en": "which allows you to add your own code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.52000000000001,
          "end": 103.46000000000001,
          "en": "on the Firebase backend which can be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.46000000000001,
          "end": 106.42,
          "en": "for incoming requests and which would allow you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.42,
          "end": 109,
          "en": "to transform data on the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109,
          "end": 112.22,
          "en": "So it would be possible to integrate this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.22,
          "end": 115.68,
          "en": "And if you're using your own backend built with Node.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.68,
          "end": 119.96000000000001,
          "en": "or PHP or whatever if you build your own backend API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.96000000000001,
          "end": 123.34,
          "en": "then of course you're also totally free to add code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.34,
          "end": 127.43,
          "en": "on that backend API that does more with the incoming data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.43,
          "end": 129.763,
          "en": "than just store it in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.74,
          "end": 134.91,
          "en": "But since this is no course about backend API development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.91,
          "end": 137.57999999999998,
          "en": "and about backend programming languages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.57999999999998,
          "end": 140.31,
          "en": "that's not the route I will take here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.31,
          "end": 143.37,
          "en": "It's something you can do but it requires knowledge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.37,
          "end": 148.16,
          "en": "about backend programming languages like Node.js or PHP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.16,
          "end": 151,
          "en": "And we don't have that here in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151,
          "end": 153.67000000000002,
          "en": "Therefore it's important to recognize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.67000000000002,
          "end": 156.68,
          "en": "that the code we need to write on the frontend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.68,
          "end": 160.09,
          "en": "and where we write dead code will depend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.09,
          "end": 162.17000000000002,
          "en": "on our backend code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.17000000000002,
          "end": 165.03,
          "en": "Because we of course have our backend API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.03,
          "end": 169.38,
          "en": "our backend server talking to our frontend application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.38,
          "end": 171.7,
          "en": "with help of these http requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.7,
          "end": 174.51,
          "en": "and the responses which we send around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.51,
          "end": 179.21,
          "en": "Now if we would have a backend API that does a lot of work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.21,
          "end": 182.22,
          "en": "so that does not just store incoming data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.22,
          "end": 183.95,
          "en": "but also transform it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.95,
          "end": 188.65,
          "en": "If we had an API like this then our frontend application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.65,
          "end": 190.38,
          "en": "could do less work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.38,
          "end": 194.14,
          "en": "It could just send data like data for a product",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.14,
          "end": 196.03,
          "en": "that should be added to a cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.03,
          "end": 198.72,
          "en": "It could send that data to the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.72,
          "end": 201.22,
          "en": "lets the backend do the transformation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.22,
          "end": 204,
          "en": "and then use the response on the frontend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204,
          "end": 207.91,
          "en": "to then just there hand it off to the reducer for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.91,
          "end": 210.23,
          "en": "to store that response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.23,
          "end": 213.52,
          "en": "So then we could slim down our reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213.52,
          "end": 216.56,
          "en": "and basically just take the incoming data which is coming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.56,
          "end": 219.53,
          "en": "from the backend and which was transformed there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 219.53,
          "end": 223.62,
          "en": "so let's say the final card we could just take that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.62,
          "end": 227.71,
          "en": "and store that in Redux that's something we could do then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 227.71,
          "end": 230.48,
          "en": "But that's not the scenario we have here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 230.48,
          "end": 233.68,
          "en": "for the reasons mentioned a couple of seconds ago.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.68,
          "end": 236.55,
          "en": "Instead here we have a backend that does not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.55,
          "end": 238.41,
          "en": "do a lot of work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 238.41,
          "end": 242.17,
          "en": "It basically just stores incoming data in the format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.17,
          "end": 243.87,
          "en": "It receives it in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.87,
          "end": 246.67,
          "en": "And that means that we do need to do more work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.67,
          "end": 247.822,
          "en": "on the frontend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 247.822,
          "end": 251.78,
          "en": "There we don't just need to store data in the Redox store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.78,
          "end": 254.21,
          "en": "we also need to prepare that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.21,
          "end": 256.55,
          "en": "We need to transform the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 256.55,
          "end": 259.73,
          "en": "So exactly what we're doing here in add item to cart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.73,
          "end": 261.93,
          "en": "and in remove item from cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 261.93,
          "end": 265.36,
          "en": "We are not just getting the finished cart as a payload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 265.36,
          "end": 267.74,
          "en": "on the action instead we get a product",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 267.74,
          "end": 270.51,
          "en": "and we need to find out how to add it to the cart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 270.51,
          "end": 272.32,
          "en": "here in this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 272.32,
          "end": 274.49,
          "en": "And the same for removing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 274.49,
          "end": 278.83,
          "en": "And that's no problem and it of course makes 100% sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 278.83,
          "end": 282.23,
          "en": "if we have no backend but if we do have a backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 282.23,
          "end": 284.61,
          "en": "it is at least something to be aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 284.61,
          "end": 286.51,
          "en": "that depending on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 286.51,
          "end": 288.87,
          "en": "and the amount of work the backend does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 288.87,
          "end": 291.33,
          "en": "we could do less work here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 291.33,
          "end": 294.33,
          "en": "if the backend would do the work for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 294.33,
          "end": 297.72,
          "en": "But as mentioned multiple times, that's not the case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 297.72,
          "end": 299.99,
          "en": "and therefore we will need to find a way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 299.99,
          "end": 303.3,
          "en": "to still do the work here on the frontend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 303.3,
          "end": 305.89,
          "en": "and at the same time then send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 305.89,
          "end": 308.383,
          "en": "that transformed data to the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 308.383,
          "end": 313.11,
          "en": "without doing that sending inside of the reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 313.11,
          "end": 316.95,
          "en": "because we learned that we're not allowed to do it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 316.95,
          "end": 320.4,
          "en": "So that's the problem set with which we have to work here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 320.4,
          "end": 324.99,
          "en": "And therefore let's now determine where to best put our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 324.99,
          "end": 328.28,
          "en": "for sending the updated card to the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 328.28,
          "end": 331.08,
          "en": "if the backend is not doing that work for us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 331.08,
          "end": 334.36,
          "en": "and we therefore have to do it here and at the same time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 334.36,
          "end": 337.1,
          "en": "we're not allowed to send our requests inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 337.1,
          "end": 338.603,
          "en": "of the reducer function.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}